Subject: Console does not accept custom scripts / 
feature request for player stat system

Hello Valve,

I am writing about the CS2 developer console. When I try to 
enter custom commands or scripts into the console, I receive 
"Unknown command" errors. The console only accepts built-in 
Source 2 engine commands and rejects any custom logic.

Request / Issue:
1. Please clarify whether custom scripting in the in-game 
   console is supported at all.
2. It would be great to have an official way for players to 
   track personal stats (aim, movement, reflex training) 
   directly in-game, similar to a progression/leveling system.

Steps to reproduce:
1. Open CS2 console (~ key).
2. Type any custom command, e.g. "Player.train".
3. Console returns: Unknown command.

System info:
- Game: Counter-Strike 2 (Prime Status Upgrade)
- OS: Windows
- Purchase date: July 12

Thank you for your time.   




Subject: Feature Request - New Grenade Type "Black Flash" 
(Reverse Flashbang) + Update Request

Hello Valve Team,

I am a CS2 player (Prime Status, purchased July 12) and I 
would like to submit a feature request for an upcoming update.

REQUEST: A new grenade type called "Black Flash" 
(a reverse / dark flashbang).

How it should work:
- The current white flashbang blinds players with a bright 
  WHITE screen (overexposure).
- The new "Black Flash" would blind players the opposite way: 
  the screen turns completely BLACK (total darkness), blocking 
  vision instead of overexposing it.
- Same mechanics as the classic flashbang: same fuse time, 
  same blast radius, same blind duration — only the visual 
  effect is inverted (white -> black).

Why this would be good for the game:
1. Adds a new tactical layer — teams could mix white and black 
   flashes for different strategies.
2. It creates counter-play: smart positioning against a black 
   flash would feel fresh and skill-based.
3. Two NEW features from one idea:
   - Feature 1: The Black Flash grenade itself.
   - Feature 2: A new utility slot / loadout choice, letting 
     players pick White Flash OR Black Flash before the round.

This would bring something genuinely new to CS2 while keeping 
the core gameplay fair and balanced.

Thank you very much for reading my suggestion. I hope the team 
considers it!

System info:
- Game: Counter-Strike 2 (Prime Status Upgrade)
- OS: Windows

